>>> STEP 3b  LOAD SWEEP: at what traffic does sequencing matter?
  At the calibrated arrival rate (about 24 rakes/month, against
  TERI's 15/month for an average one-line terminal) the PHYSICAL
  model is lightly loaded and no sequencing rule can help. That is
  itself the Layer 0 finding: the physical layer is not the
  bottleneck at realistic Indian siding throughput. Sequencing only
  earns its keep once the line is genuinely contended - which is
  what the administrative layer causes, and Layer 1 shows.
